IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `crtpa-kleene`
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `sgia-p1-definitions`

-- Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation -- LAYER 1, SECTION 1: SHORT TITLE AND APPLICATION.
--
-- What is encoded: s 1(2) and (3), the date from which the Act reaches a contract.  Both limbs of
-- s 1(3) have a rule of their own; s 1(1), the short title, is inert (machinery, reason 2).
--
-- READING A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives; NOTHING means the Act does
-- not answer on these facts (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
--
-- THE PERIOD OF 6 MONTHS (fork G1 of NOTES.md).  "The end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002"
-- is a period of months from a day.  The Interpretation Act 1965 defines "month" (calendar month, s 2(1))
-- and has no rule for counting a period of months from a day (staged module `sgia-interpretation-time`,
-- whose header says so), so its answer here is NOTHING and is asserted to be.  A period counted with the
-- first day inside it ends at the end of 30 June 2002; one counted without it ends at the end of
-- 1 July 2002.  A contract entered into on or before 30 June 2002 is before the end of the period on
-- both counts, and one entered into on or after 2 July 2002 is after it on both; a contract entered into
-- on 1 July 2002 is the one the text does not decide, and the answer for it is NOTHING.

§ `Section 1 -- the Interpretation Act's count of the six months`

-- (Interpretation Act text, lines 406 and 2146-2170, as the staged module quotes them): the Act defines
-- "month" and "year" and gives no rule for a period of months from a day.
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 1(2) the last day of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002, as the Interpretation Act counts it` MEANS
    `the last day of a period` (Date 1 1 2002) 6 Months From EMPTY FALSE

§ `Section 1(2) -- the contract was entered into before the end of the period`

-- src:41 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), this Act does not apply in relation to a
-- src:42 | contract entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from
-- src:43 | 1 January 2002.
@ref s 1(2) (src:41-43)
GIVEN `the date the contract was entered into` IS A DATE
      `the Interpretation Act's last day of the period` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1(2) the contract was entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Interpretation Act's last day of the period`
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN JUST (`the date the contract was entered into` AT MOST lastDay)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        BRANCH
            -- before the end of the period on either count of it
            IF `the date the contract was entered into` AT MOST (Date 30 6 2002) THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002" is a period of months from a day, which neither this Act nor the Interpretation Act counts; it ends at the end of 30 June 2002 or of 1 July 2002 and the text does not choose
            IF `the date the contract was entered into` EQUALS (Date 1 7 2002) THEN NOTHING
            -- FALSE-kind (a period the text fixes in its own words): "before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002"
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `Section 1(3) -- the restriction does not apply`

-- src:48 | (a) is entered into on or after 1 January 2002; and
@ref s 1(3)(a) (src:48-48)
GIVEN `the date the contract was entered into` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1(3)(a) the contract is entered into on or after 1 January 2002` MEANS
    `the date the contract was entered into` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 2002)

-- src:50 | (b) expressly provides for the application of this Act.
@ref s 1(3)(b) (src:50-50)
GIVEN `the contract expressly provides for the application of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1(3)(b) the contract expressly provides for the application of this Act` MEANS
    `the contract expressly provides for the application of this Act`

-- src:45 | (3) The restriction in subsection (2) does not apply in relation to a
-- src:46 | contract which —
-- src:48 | (a) is entered into on or after 1 January 2002; and
-- src:50 | (b) expressly provides for the application of this Act.
@ref s 1(3) (src:45-50)
GIVEN `the date the contract was entered into` IS A DATE
      `the contract expressly provides for the application of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1(3) the restriction in subsection (2) does not apply in relation to the contract` MEANS
    IF `s 1(3)(a) the contract is entered into on or after 1 January 2002` `the date the contract was entered into`
       AND `s 1(3)(b) the contract expressly provides for the application of this Act` `the contract expressly provides for the application of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 1(3) lifts the restriction only for "a contract which" meets (a) and (b); it does not say the restriction applies to any other contract, which is s 1(2)'s business
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 1(2) with (3) -- does the restriction bite, and does the Act apply`

-- The restriction itself, as a yes/no (the "bar" of NOTES.md fork G2): JUST TRUE when s 1(2) holds the
-- contract out of the Act, JUST FALSE when s 1(3) lifts it or the contract is after the period.
-- src:41 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), this Act does not apply in relation to a
-- src:42 | contract entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from
-- src:43 | 1 January 2002.
-- src:45 | (3) The restriction in subsection (2) does not apply in relation to a
-- src:46 | contract which —
-- src:48 | (a) is entered into on or after 1 January 2002; and
-- src:50 | (b) expressly provides for the application of this Act.
@ref s 1(2) and (3) (src:41-50)
GIVEN `the date the contract was entered into` IS A DATE
      `the contract expressly provides for the application of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1(2) the restriction on the application of this Act applies to the contract` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The restriction in subsection (2) does not apply in relation to a contract which — (a) is entered into on or after 1 January 2002; and (b) expressly provides for the application of this Act."
        IF `s 1(3) the restriction in subsection (2) does not apply in relation to the contract` `the date the contract was entered into` `the contract expressly provides for the application of this Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- the contract is before the end of the period and s 1(3) does not lift the restriction
        IF `s 1(2) the contract was entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002` `the date the contract was entered into` `s 1(2) the last day of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002, as the Interpretation Act counts it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (a period the text fixes in its own words): the restriction reaches only "a contract entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002"
        IF `s 1(2) the contract was entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002` `the date the contract was entered into` `s 1(2) the last day of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002, as the Interpretation Act counts it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the contract was entered into on 1 July 2002, and the text does not say whether that is before the end of the period of 6 months
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:41 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), this Act does not apply in relation to a
-- src:42 | contract entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from
-- src:43 | 1 January 2002.
@ref s 1(2) (src:41-43)
GIVEN `the date the contract was entered into` IS A DATE
      `the contract expressly provides for the application of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1(2) this Act applies in relation to the contract` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this Act does not apply in relation to a contract entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from 1 January 2002"
        IF `s 1(2) the restriction on the application of this Act applies to the contract` `the date the contract was entered into` `the contract expressly provides for the application of this Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (3)" lifts the restriction and s 1 says nothing affirmative; a lifted bar grants nothing (judgment call QA)
        IF `s 1(3) the restriction in subsection (2) does not apply in relation to the contract` `the date the contract was entered into` `the contract expressly provides for the application of this Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 1(2) restricts only a contract entered into before the end of the period, and does not say that this Act applies to a later contract
        IF `s 1(2) the restriction on the application of this Act applies to the contract` `the date the contract was entered into` `the contract expressly provides for the application of this Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the contract was entered into on 1 July 2002, and the text does not say whether that is before the end of the period of 6 months
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
